> THEORETICAL NOTE: Is this directly comparable to Raw Space?
> Yes. Because standardizing a linear combination mathematically distributes, the difference
> vector in this space is simply the raw difference vector divided feature-wise by the
> standard deviation. Consequently, this MSE is a *variance-weighted* version of the raw MSE.

--- 3. Z-SCORE NORMALIZED SPACE (Variance Preserving) ---
Expected: sqrt(0.5) * z'_1 + sqrt(0.5) * z'_2
Average MSE:               4.100899
Average Cosine Similarity: 0.1510
> THEORETICAL NOTE: Because z-scored embeddings have unit variance, interpolating with
> 0.5 weights causes the expected vector's variance to collapse to 0.5. Using sqrt(0.5)
> preserves the unit variance, representing a more accurate geometric midpoint in the
> normalized high-dimensional space.
